Title: Let MASM settings through gyp's MSVS-to-MSBuild conversion
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo), after sawbuck-ng patches/06-gyp-next-masm-settings.patch

  lld-link : error : <root>: undefined symbol: _winwrap_static_redirects
  [.../node.vcxproj]

gyp's MASM tool table has exactly one entry:

  _Same(_masm, "UseSafeExceptionHandlers", _boolean)  # /safeseh

and ConvertToMSBuildSettings keeps only settings present in that table.
Anything else takes the else branch, which prints

  Warning: unrecognized setting MASM/PreprocessorDefinitions

and is then never added to the output. The warning is the only trace:
generation succeeds, the project is written without the setting, and the build
does whatever it does without it.

That is not a harmless omission for an assembler. A .asm source cannot be
selected per configuration -- one generated project holds every configuration
at once -- so a library needing different assembly per architecture has to
list every variant and have each guard its own body on a define. Which is
exactly what MASM/PreprocessorDefinitions is for, and exactly what cannot be
delivered.

winwrap is that case, and 07-winwrap-xp-link.patch is what makes node.exe
depend on it. Its redirect table exists twice -- src/static_redirects.cc for
Clang, src/forwarders_{x86,x64}.asm for MSVC -- and the MASM pair guards on
WINWRAP_X86 / WINWRAP_X64. Without the define both files assemble to empty
objects, which is not a build failure: the library links, exports nothing, and
silently does none of what it exists to do. Here it surfaces one step later,
at the final link, because the anchor symbol node.exe names in /INCLUDE: sits
inside the same guard.

So this adds the three settings from masm.xml the table is missing:
PreprocessorDefinitions and IncludePaths, which are /D and /I and have no
substitute, and AdditionalOptions, the escape hatch that stops the next
missing MASM flag needing another patch.

Nothing is renamed or translated: all three have the same name in MSVS and
MSBuild, so each is a _Same line, in the same shape and alphabetical position
as the ClCompile entries above.

Worth upstreaming rather than carrying. It is additive, it matches the schema
the comment above the table already points at, and the omission looks like
nobody having needed MASM beyond /safeseh rather than a decision. sawbuck-ng
carries the identical change against its own gyp-next.

diff --git a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py
--- a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py
+++ b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/MSVSSettings.py
@@ -1280,4 +1280,7 @@
 # MSBuild MASM settings.
 
 # Options that have the same name in MSVS and MSBuild.
+_Same(_masm, "AdditionalOptions", _string_list)
+_Same(_masm, "IncludePaths", _folder_list)  # /I
+_Same(_masm, "PreprocessorDefinitions", _string_list)  # /D
 _Same(_masm, "UseSafeExceptionHandlers", _boolean)  # /safeseh
